# SUGGESTS, never Depends or Recommends — deliberately. cuems-cluster-poweroff
# and cuems-displays-on drive the cuems-power-bridge library through its venv
# interpreter, but cuems-common must stay installable and fully functional on a
# host with no bridge at all (every node, and any controller that does not want
# orderly power-off). Both scripts check for that interpreter and, if it is
# absent, log one ERROR and exit 0 — verified on test2: `systemctl stop` still
# returns 0, so a missing bridge can never fail a poweroff. The units use
# ordering (Before=/After=) and at most Wants=, which systemd ignores when the
# named unit does not exist; nothing uses Requires= or BindsTo=.
# DO NOT promote this to Depends: that would make a controller-only, opt-in
# feature a mandatory dependency of the package every node installs.
Suggests: cuems-power-bridge
Conflicts: network-manager
Breaks: cuems-nodeconf (<< 0.1.0-8)
Description: CUEMS common configuration and systemd services
 This package contains systemd service files, configuration files,
 and scripts required for CUEMS operation.
 .
 All Python scripts use /usr/lib/cuems/bin/python3 provided by
 the cuems-utils package.
 .
 network_map.xml's node_role migration (feature 007) — the cuems-utils
 version floor is the schema this package ships and converts documents to;
 the cuems-nodeconf Breaks (not a hard Depends — nodeconf is optional and
 currently disabled cluster-wide) refuses installing this package's
 conversion alongside a cuems-nodeconf still writing the retired
 <node_type> element, rather than merely documenting the ordering
 (FR-030d, SC-012). See specs/007-node-model-migration/migration-guide.md
 in cuems-utils for the full release gate this enforces one edge of.
 .
 This package requires isc-dhcp-server and hostapd for WiFi access
 point functionality (cuems-wifi.service and hostapd.service).
 .
 This package installs Apache2 site configuration files and enables
 required Apache2 modules and sites. Module files are provided by their
 respective Debian packages (libapache2-mod-*).
 .
 This package conflicts with network-manager and, as the whole cuems ecosystem,
 it is not intended to be used on desktop environments.
